  "query_preview": "..FOR EXTREME SOUTHWESTERN CALIFORNIA INCLUDING ORANGE...\nSAN DIEGO...WESTERN RIVERSIDE AND SOUTHWESTERN SAN BERNARDINO\nCOUNTIES...\n\n\n...UPDATED AVIATION DISCUSSION...\n\nThis morning featured clouds in all levels of the troposphere. \nPatchy fog covered San Diego County west of I-15 earlier in the \nmorning, making way to photogenic skies of cumulus, altocumulus, and \ncirrus embedded with a few virga showers (sprinkles were reported in \ninland parts of San Diego). While these clouds signal to plentiful \nmid-level moisture, the broad coverage in SD County might be \ndelaying convection over the mountains and thus shower/tstorm \nactivity until later in the afternoon. Meanwhile, cumulus clouds \nhave been persistently building on the eastern slopes of the San \nBernardino and Riverside County mountains with some showers \ndeveloping. More showers and thunderstorms are likely over these \nslopes through around 7 PM this evening. Any thunderstorm that \ndevelops could bring heavy downpours and up to an inch of rain \nlocally.\n\n\nTemperatures this afternoon are generally running a few degrees \ncooler than yesterday, expecting to reach the mid-90s inland, \n100- 105F in the IE and 106-110F in the lower deserts. Highs today\nare expected to be the noticeably the coolest for the week for \nthe inland valleys and lower deserts. \n\nThunderstorm chances peak this afternoon as PWAT's fall through \nWednesday, though isolated terrain driven shower/t-storm chances \nremain in the forecast for our mountains through Thursday as the mid-\nlevel flow remains southerly, tapping into modest mid-level \nmoisture.\n\nThe ridge axis over the Desert Southwest shifts westward through the \nmiddle of the week and high temperatures peak Wednesday through \nFriday through Southern California. Highs are expected to reach the \nupper 90s to 105F in the inland valleys, 103-108F through the IE and \nup to 115F in the lower deserts. \n\nBoth the GFS and the ECMWF show a significant flattening of the \nridge over the weekend, increasing confidence that temperatures will \nreturn closer to normal by early next week.\n\n\nIn the meantime, take breaks in the shade, hydrate and seek A/C when \npossible!",
